# Review: TrelloPlugin

Discovery, pull and push are built and well tested. `GetTrelloBoards` lists open boards and creates
nothing; `reconcileBoardCards` does the three-way merge (remote wins on conflict), soft-deletes
closed or missing cards and orders columns by list `pos`; `pushBoardCards` POSTs new cards and PUTs
only diverged fields. `sync.test.ts` and `handlers.test.ts` cover all of that against a stubbed API.
The Trello client retries only transport failures, 429 and 5xx, and parses `<key>:<token>`.

Of 31 items: 20 done, 6 untested, 2 partial, 1 diverged, 2 missing. Findings:

- **Materialization moved out of sync.** The Kanban is created eagerly by a third operation,
  `MaterializeTrelloTarget`, when a board is bound; `SyncTrelloBoard` returns zero counts when the
  binding has no Kanban. The spec has no op block for it.
- **Token parsing and retry policy have no tests.** `credentialsFromToken` and `shouldRetry` are
  stubbed out by `handlers.test.ts`'s module mock, so T-8 and F-6.1/F-6.2 are unverified.
- **The sync op's shape drifted.** It takes `connection` and `priority` (no `kanban`), fans out over
  bindings, and fails with `ConnectorSync.DatabaseMissingError` rather than the named spec errors.

